This newly added prop comment only restates the member name and type: "Callback" echoes the function type and "on layout" restates `onLayout`. It names no unit, default, boundary condition, null/undefined semantics, ownership, invariant, or distinction from a sibling, so it adds nothing over the self-explanatory name and type. (The sibling `report` and `policy` comments are fine because they add facts.)

Delete the comment and leave the self-explanatory prop undocumented:

```tsx
    /** The workspace the report belongs to */
    policy: OnyxEntry<OnyxTypes.Policy>;

    onLayout?: (event: LayoutChangeEvent) => void;
```

The comment on `CampfireField.id` says "Unique identifier of the account", but this member belongs to `CampfireField`, not an account (copy-paste from `CampfireAccount`). Fix the wording to describe the field, or remove it since `id: string` on `CampfireField` is self-explanatory:

```ts
/** Unique identifier of the field. */
id: string;
```

The comment on `CampfireSubsidiary.id` says "Unique identifier of the account", but this member belongs to `CampfireSubsidiary`, not an account — it looks copy-pasted from `CampfireAccount`. A comment that misdescribes the member is worse than none; the following `name`/`currency` comments have the same "account" wording.

Correct the wording so it describes the subsidiary, or drop it if the name/type are already self-explanatory:

```ts
/** Unique identifier of the subsidiary. */
id: string;
```

In the first union branch of `MenuItemPrimaryTextProps`, the `children` prop is left undocumented while the `children` prop in the other branch has a `/** */` block comment. Document `children` here too so both branches carry a doc block.

Example:
```tsx
| {
      /** Plain text to render as the primary content */
      children: string | number;

      accessibilityLabel?: never;
  }
```

In `MenuItemSupportingTextProps`, the `children` prop is left undocumented while its sibling `numberOfLines` has a `/** */` block comment. Every prop should carry a `/** */` doc block.

Add a block comment above `children`, e.g.:
```tsx
type MenuItemSupportingTextProps = {
    /** Text to render */
    children: string | number;

    /** Defaults to 2. Supporting text wraps, unlike primary text, which is always one line */
    numberOfLines?: number;
};
```

In `NumericFieldProps`, several props (`onInputChange`, `onBlur`, `onSubmitEditing`, `ref`, `children`) are left undocumented while their siblings (`value`, `allowNegative`, `decimals`, `maxLength`, `errorText`, `numericEditingRef`) each carry a `/** ... */` block. Per STYLE.md every prop should be documented with a block comment, and mixing documented and undocumented props next to each other is exactly the case this rule catches.

Add a `/** ... */` block above each undocumented prop, e.g.:

```tsx
/** Called with the canonical value whenever the user commits an edit. */
onInputChange?: (value: string) => void;
```

The new `currentUserAccountID` prop is added to `CompleteOnboardingProps` with no `/** */` block comment, while its sibling props in the same type (`conciergeChat`, `adminsChatReport`, `selfDMReport`, `shouldSkipConciergeOnboarding`) are all documented with `/** */` blocks. Per STYLE.md, every component/type prop should carry a `/** */` block, and an undocumented prop sitting next to documented siblings should be documented.

Add a block comment describing the prop:

```ts
    /** Whether onboarding is handled outside the Concierge DM, so no message, tasks, or sign-off should be posted there. */
    shouldSkipConciergeOnboarding?: boolean;

    /** The account ID of the current user, used to build the onboarding Onyx data. */
    currentUserAccountID: number;
```

`ref` is left undocumented while its sibling props in `HeaderTooltipIconButtonProps` all have `/** ... */` block comments. Add a matching block comment.

```tsx
    /** Forwarded ref to the underlying pressable */
    ref?: PressableRef;
```

`shouldUseHeadlineHeader` is left undocumented while its sibling props in `HeaderTitleProps` all have `/** ... */` block comments. Add a matching block comment so every prop is documented consistently.

```tsx
    /** Whether the header uses the taller headline style */
    shouldUseHeadlineHeader: boolean;
```

The new `shouldPreserveBroaderCarousel` prop is added to `NavigateToTransactionThreadParams` with no documentation, while every one of its sibling props (`transactionID`, `reportActions`, `report`, `transaction`, `siblingTransactionIDs`, `backTo`) is documented with a `/** ... */` block. An undocumented prop sitting next to documented siblings should carry its own `/** */` block comment.

Add a block comment above the prop, for example:

```tsx
/** When true, keep an already-active broader carousel (e.g. the Spend page's list) instead of re-seeding it with just this report's siblings */
shouldPreserveBroaderCarousel?: boolean;
```

In the new `VictoryChartScaledProviderProps` type, `scale` is documented with a `/** */` block but its sibling `children` is left undocumented. Per STYLE.md, every prop in a `Props` type should carry a `/** */` block comment when sibling props are documented.

Add a JSDoc block above `children`:

```tsx
type VictoryChartScaledProviderProps = {
    /** Uniform factor to scale all pixel-space chart config by (may be > 1) */
    scale: number;

    /** Chart sub-tree to re-provide the scaled context to */
    children: React.ReactNode;
};
```

The newly added `DirectionsProps` type documents its props (`directionCoordinates`, `alternateDirection`, `setIsAlternateDirectionSelected`, `distanceInMeters`, `unit`, `waypoints`) with `//` line comments. Per `STYLE.md`, props of a `...Props` type must be documented with `/** ... */` block comments, not `//`.

Convert each prop comment to a block comment, e.g.:

```ts
type DirectionsProps = {
    /** List of coordinates which together forms a direction. */
    directionCoordinates?: Coordinate[] | Coordinate[][];

    /** List of coordinates which together forms an alternate direction. */
    alternateDirection?: AlternateDirection;
    // ...
};
```

The newly added `DistanceSymbolProps` type documents its props (`distanceInMeters`, `distanceUnit`, `toggleDistanceUnit`, `directionCoordinates`, `waypoints`, `isSelected`) with `//` line comments. Per `STYLE.md`, component/prop members of a `...Props` type must be documented with `/** ... */` block comments, not `//`.

Convert each prop comment to a block comment, e.g.:

```ts
type DistanceSymbolProps = {
    /** Distance displayed on the map in meters. */
    distanceInMeters?: number;

    /** Unit of measurement for distance. */
    distanceUnit?: Unit;
    // ...
};
```

Component props must be documented with a `/** ... */` block comment, not a `//` line comment. The newly added `shouldDisableButtonWhenOffline` prop uses a `//` comment above it, which does not follow the JSDoc style guidelines from `STYLE.md`.

Convert the `//` comment to a JSDoc block comment:

```tsx
/** An optional boolean indicating whether the import button should be disabled while offline. Defaults to true. */
shouldDisableButtonWhenOffline?: boolean;
```

This changed prop in the `AnimatedSubmitButtonProps` type is documented with a `//` line comment. Per `STYLE.md`, component props must be documented with a `/** ... */` block comment above each prop, not a `//` comment. A sibling prop in this same type (`isMarkAsDone`) already uses the `/** */` block form, so this one should match.

```tsx
    /** Submit buttons support the default and success styles; danger is not a valid submit state. */
    variant?: typeof CONST.BUTTON_VARIANT.SUCCESS;
```

The newly added `primaryAction` and `backTo` props on `MoneyReportHeaderMoreContentProps` have no JSDoc block, while their sibling props (`statusBarType`, `shouldShowNextStep`, `shouldRenderActionsInRow`) are documented with `/** ... */` blocks. Props should be documented consistently.

Add a `/** ... */` block above each:

```tsx
/** The report's primary action, forwarded to the actions row */
primaryAction: MoneyReportHeaderActionsProps['primaryAction'];

/** Route to navigate back to */
backTo: Route | undefined;
```

The new `isStale` prop on `SpendSummaryRowProps` is documented with a `//` line comment. Per STYLE.md, component props must be documented with a `/** ... */` block comment above the member, not a `//` comment.

```tsx
    /** Greys the total when a queued offline change may have made it stale. */
    isStale?: boolean;
```

The newly added `shouldUseFixedPopoverHeight` prop has no `/** */` block comment, yet its sibling props in this `SingleSelectProps` type (`items`, `isSearchable`, `searchPlaceholder`, `shouldShowList`, `itemHeight`) are documented with JSDoc blocks. Per STYLE.md every prop should carry a `/** */` block so its purpose is clear at the definition site.

Add a JSDoc block above the prop:

```tsx
/** Whether the popover should keep a fixed height while filtering results */
shouldUseFixedPopoverHeight?: boolean;
```

The new `action` member is added to the `SearchQueryItem` type with no `/** ... */` block comment, while a sibling member in the same type (`shouldIconApplyFill`) is documented with a `/** */` block. Props should be documented consistently with a block comment describing their purpose.

Add a JSDoc block above the new prop:

```tsx
/** Callback invoked to navigate to the destination when this navigation suggestion row is selected */
action?: () => void;
```

The newly added `excludeBankAccountID` prop is documented with a plain `/* ... */` block comment while its sibling props in the `PaymentMethodListProps` type use `/** ... */` JSDoc blocks (e.g. `excludeStates` directly above it). Per the JSDoc style guidelines, component props must be documented with a `/** */` block comment.

Change the comment to a JSDoc block:

```tsx
/** Bank account ID of an account that we do not want to show (i.e. it's already connected) */
excludeBankAccountID?: number;
```
